  "asr_text_clean": "The ship was old, its wooden frame creaking in the cold, dark water. He stood at the helm, hands trembling, clutching a rusted compass. The destination was written in faded ink on a map he\u2019d memorized years ago\u2014a place no chart could trace. The crew whispered of curses, of storms that swallowed ships whole. But he knew the truth: the treasure wasn\u2019t gold. It was the journey itself, the defiance of giving up, even when the world said he\u2019d already lost everything. The engines roared, steady as a heartbeat. And he sailed, not toward safety, but toward the edge of the known world, where the sea whispered secrets only the brave\u2014or the desperate\u2014could hear.",
